cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DETOX, please cite it as below."
title: "DETOX: Runtime Defense for Vision-Language-Action Models under Attack"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Yun
    given-names: Sangho
    affiliation: POSTECH
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Minsoo
    affiliation: POSTECH
  - family-names: Yu
    given-names: Hwanjo
    affiliation: POSTECH
date-released: "2026-11-23"
url: "https://devsangho.github.io/DETOX-public/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/devsangho/DETOX-public"
abstract: >-
  DETOX is a runtime defense for vision-language-action robot policies. It reads
  only the robot's own trusted telemetry and replaces the next command with a hold
  before a backdoored or hijacked policy drops an object, pushes a bystander, or
  moves too fast.
keywords:
  - VLA safety
  - VLA defense
  - vision-language-action
  - VLA backdoor
  - backdoor attack
  - runtime defense
  - runtime monitoring
  - trusted telemetry
  - harm prevention
  - anomaly detection
  - conformal calibration
